@host = http://localhost:5243

### No token: 401 with a problem document, and a WWW-Authenticate header.
GET {{host}}/api/whoami

### Obtain a service-to-service token from the demo provider, described rather than returned.
GET {{host}}/api/token

### Anonymous is answered rather than refused.
GET {{host}}/api/whoami-or-anonymous

### An unreachable provider: 503 unavailable, because waiting may help.
GET {{host}}/api/downstream-unreachable

### A wrong authority: 500 internal, because waiting will not.
GET {{host}}/api/downstream-misconfigured

### With a token, /api/whoami reports the client rather than a subject, because a client credentials
### grant has no resource owner to name. Paste an access token from /api/token into the header below —
### it is not returned by that endpoint, so take it from the provider directly:
###   curl -s -u m2m:secret -d grant_type=client_credentials -d scope=api \
###        https://demo.duendesoftware.com/connect/token
GET {{host}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
